        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(doctor): keep failure report truncation UTF-16 safe",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where failure reports in doctor session-sqlite migration could contain broken surrogate characters when the 500-char truncation boundary fell inside an emoji or other multi-code-unit character.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe existing `.slice(0, 500)` call does not account for UTF-16 surrogate pairs. Replacing it with `truncateUtf16Safe` ensures that multi-code-unit characters are kept intact or dropped entirely. The fix also adds a visible `... [truncated]` suffix when truncation occurs, making it clear to operators that the output was shortened.\n\n## User Impact\n\nDoctor failure reports containing emoji, CJK, or other non-BMP characters in path names, agent IDs, or error descriptions remain well-formed when truncated.\n\n## Evidence\n\nExecuted a replicate of `sanitizeFailureReportText` (with `truncateUtf16Safe`) against 5 edge cases at the 500-char boundary. All pass — zero lone surrogates in output.\n\n```\n--- Under 500 chars ---\nInput length: 93\nOutput length: 93\nEnds with: ...aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\nHas lone surrogate: NO\nStatus: PASS\n\n--- Emoji at 500-char boundary (dropped) ---\nInput length: 504\nOutput length: 500\nEnds with: ...xxxxxxxxxxxxxxx... [truncated]\nHas lone surrogate: NO\nStatus: PASS\n\n--- Emoji within limit (preserved) ---\nInput length: 503\nOutput length: 500\nEnds with: ...yyyyyyyyyyyyyyy... [truncated]\nHas lone surrogate: NO\nStatus: PASS\n\n--- Multiple emoji ---\nInput length: 556\nOutput length: 500\nEnds with: ...wwwwwwwwwwwwwww... [truncated]\nHas lone surrogate: NO\nStatus: PASS\n\n--- CJK at boundary ---\nInput length: 500\nOutput length: 500\nEnds with: ...aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa中文\nHas lone surrogate: NO\nStatus: PASS\n\nCOMMAND_EXIT_CODE=0\n```\n\nScript: `scripts/evidence-doctor.ts` (inlines `truncateUtf16Safe` from `@openclaw/normalization-core/utf16-slice`; replicates actual `sanitizeFailureReportText` as defined in `src/commands/doctor-session-sqlite-migration-run.ts`).\n\n**Result**: All 5 scenarios PASS. No lone surrogates produced at any boundary condition.",
